2. What is multithreading? What is its practical use in your project? What are the alternatives?

→ Multithreading means executing multiple tasks concurrently using different threads.
→ In my LabFlow project, concurrent processing can help handle multiple requests and independent tasks efficiently.
→ Alternatives include ExecutorService, CompletableFuture, Java 21 virtual threads, and asynchronous Kafka processing.
→ I choose the approach based on workload, ordering requirements, and whether tasks are CPU-bound or I/O-bound.

