4. How do you handle transaction rollback when a connected microservice fails?

→ If the remote service fails before my local transaction commits, I can propagate the exception so Spring rolls back the local transaction.
→ @Transactional rolls back the local database transaction; it cannot automatically undo a transaction already committed by another microservice.
→ For distributed business transactions, I use the Saga pattern with compensating actions.
→ For reliable asynchronous communication, I use the Transactional Outbox pattern, Kafka retries, and idempotent consumers.

