7. What are Default and OnPush change detection strategies?

→ Default checks the component tree during normal Angular change-detection cycles.
→ OnPush allows Angular to skip checking a component subtree until a relevant trigger occurs.
→ Triggers include changed input values, events, and updates to Signals read by the template.
→ OnPush can improve performance in large applications when inputs and state updates are handled correctly.

