8. Explain switchMap, mergeMap, and concatMap.

→ switchMap cancels the previous inner subscription when a new value arrives. Use it for search suggestions.
→ mergeMap runs inner operations concurrently. Use it for independent requests that can run in parallel.
→ concatMap processes operations sequentially in order. Use it when one operation must finish before the next begins.
→ Easy memory trick: switchMap = latest wins; mergeMap = parallel; concatMap = one by one.

